<section class="cxx entity method">

  <h1 id="Arcadia_ByteArray_isResizable">Arcadia_ByteArray_isResizable</h1>

  <my-signature><code>
  Arcadia_BooleanValue<br>
  Arcadia_ByteArray_isResizable<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;(<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arcadia_Thread* thread,<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arcadia_ByteArray const* self<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;)
  </code></my-signature>

  <my-summary>Determines whether this byte array supports changing its logical size.</my-summary>

  <section class="cxx parameters">
    <h1>Parameters</h1>
    <div>
      <div><code>Arcadia_Thread* thread</code></div>
      <div>A pointer to the calling thread.</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div><code>Arcadia_ByteArray const* self</code></div>
      <div>A pointer to this byte array.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cxx return-value">
    <h1>Return value</h1>
    <p><code>Arcadia_BooleanValue_True</code> if this instance supports <code>resize</code>; <code>Arcadia_BooleanValue_False</code> otherwise.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cxx remarks">
    <h1>Remarks</h1>
    <p>The result is stable throughout this instance's lifetime. Resizability is independent of mutability and contiguity. A fixed-size array rejects <code>resize</code> even when the requested size equals its current size.</p>
  </section>

</section>
